In this example, we have defined the variables `total_revenue`, `cost_of_goods_sold`, `operating_expenses`, and `taxes` with sample values. We then use these variables to calculate the profit using the formula `profit = total_revenue - cost_of_goods_sold - operating_expenses - taxes`. Finally, we display the current profit to the store owner using the `print()` function.
You can modify this code to retrieve the data from your store's records and update the profit value in real-time. You can also add more features to the application, such as generating reports and graphs to help the store owner analyze the profit trends over time.
